<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Titus Didius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 89 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Titus Didius was a Roman general, consul in 98 BCE and then governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, where he campaigned against the Celtiberians for several years. He forced the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiermes">Termes</a> to leave their hilltop for an unfortified site and celebrated a triumph in 93 BCE. He was killed in 89 BCE fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s Italian allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a>.</p></div>
